(703795, 74171, 19841, '<td valign="top">Since the sky whited out on you, you might as well crop the top down a bit and get the machine out of the center of the picture.   Filling the frame with more darks adds mass.</td>', 'Since the sky whited out on you, you might as well crop the top down a bit and get the machine out of the center of the picture.   Filling the frame with more darks adds mass.', '2004-05-07 10:18:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(703796, 73217, 4285, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background	6<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing	5<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.	6<br/>How well does it meet the challenge:	5<br/>Total Averaged Rating(Rounded)	6<br/>In any other challenge B and W would have worked, but without the colour the rust is pretty much hidden.</td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background	6Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing	5Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.	6How well does it meet the challenge:	5Total Averaged Rating(Rounded)	6In any other challenge B and W would have worked, but without the colour the rust is pretty much hidden.', '2004-05-07 10:20:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(703799, 74272, 15152, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. A bit off center. A nice blue sky would have been nice buy what can you do about that. I think I would have cropped it at the sky line. The lines from the tracks carry your eye to the horizon but there really isn''t any thing there on interest and its blurry from the shallow DOF. You can kind of see what it would have looked like my scrolling the top part of the photo off the screen.<br/> <br/>If you didn''t want to center it maybe a more exaggerated offset to the upper right corner would have been good too. I''m not sure centering it would have been quite right because the tracks aren''t really symmetrical.</td>', 'Nice shot. A bit off center. A nice blue sky would have been nice buy what can you do about that. I think I would have cropped it at the sky line. The lines from the tracks carry your eye to the horizon but there really isn''t any thing there on interest and its blurry from the shallow DOF. You can kind of see what it would have looked like my scrolling the top part of the photo off the screen. If you didn''t want to center it maybe a more exaggerated offset to the upper right corner would have been good too. I''m not sure centering it would have been quite right because the tracks aren''t really symmetrical.', '2004-05-07 10:23:22.000000', NULL, 1),
