(710160, 73751, 12733, '<td valign="top">This makes an interesting abstract. Nice exposure, framing and composition.</td>', 'This makes an interesting abstract. Nice exposure, framing and composition.', '2004-05-10 21:55:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(710164, 74159, 3080, '<td valign="top">I think that this may have been a good idea for the challenge, but a few things are keeping this from being a good image, in my opinion.  first off, the focus seems to be off on the entire image.  I can''t really find a strong sharp focus, and soft focus doesn''t work here.   I''m thinking a few things happened with that.  First off, see the bottom of the chain on the left side?  It looks like some motion blurr there.  Which could be the same reason that the rest of the image looks soft.  Low lighting or camera shake can both be reasons for this.  Since the background seems darker, and there are dark shadows, I''m guess that lighting was the main problem here.  Second, the rings are way too distracting in the shot.  I don''t really like the shadows, they seem kind of ''snapshotty''.  I guess it just doesn''t look like you nurtured your photo, add a bit of lighting, maybe try a tripod to reduce camera shake, and clean up the photo.  The rings are cluttering.  While there is nothing wrong with the imperfections in the skin, I do find that they draw attention away from the rusty chains which are really suposed to be the subject here.  So, while I like the idea, I think that this feels rushed, and snapshotty.  Sorry to be long winded...hope this helps some.  ~Heather~</td>', 'I think that this may have been a good idea for the challenge, but a few things are keeping this from being a good image, in my opinion.  first off, the focus seems to be off on the entire image.  I can''t really find a strong sharp focus, and soft focus doesn''t work here.   I''m thinking a few things happened with that.  First off, see the bottom of the chain on the left side?  It looks like some motion blurr there.  Which could be the same reason that the rest of the image looks soft.  Low lighting or camera shake can both be reasons for this.  Since the background seems darker, and there are dark shadows, I''m guess that lighting was the main problem here.  Second, the rings are way too distracting in the shot.  I don''t really like the shadows, they seem kind of ''snapshotty''.  I guess it just doesn''t look like you nurtured your photo, add a bit of lighting, maybe try a tripod to reduce camera shake, and clean up the photo.  The rings are cluttering.  While there is nothing wrong with the imperfections in the skin, I do find that they draw attention away from the rusty chains which are really suposed to be the subject here.  So, while I like the idea, I think that this feels rushed, and snapshotty.  Sorry to be long winded...hope this helps some.  ~Heather~', '2004-05-10 21:57:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(710165, 74272, 7703, '<td valign="top">Don''t like this one because you are propable trying to get some simetry but it''s not perfect so it looks not good to me. The sky is also to bright.</td>', 'Don''t like this one because you are propable trying to get some simetry but it''s not perfect so it looks not good to me. The sky is also to bright.', '2004-05-10 21:57:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(710166, 73787, 12733, '<td valign="top">It''s definitely rusted. Nice choice of framing (from the bit of fencing in the upper left corner, it looks like you were kind of pushed into position to avoid distractions) and good color and texture renditions. I think I would have cropped the right-hand fence door to tighten it up some more.</td>', 'It''s definitely rusted. Nice choice of framing (from the bit of fencing in the upper left corner, it looks like you were kind of pushed into position to avoid distractions) and good color and texture renditions. I think I would have cropped the right-hand fence door to tighten it up some more.', '2004-05-10 21:57:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(710168, 73269, 12733, '<td valign="top">Does the fork lift still work? Those chains look to be in really bad shape. And very rusty.</td>', 'Does the fork lift still work? Those chains look to be in really bad shape. And very rusty.', '2004-05-10 21:59:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(710172, 74020, 12733, '<td valign="top">Nice to see some action in a picture, along with plenty of rust.</td>', 'Nice to see some action in a picture, along with plenty of rust.', '2004-05-10 22:01:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(710177, 73807, 19507, '<td valign="top">I like the shot, but I have a hard time figuring out exactly how it fits in the rust category -- except maybe figuratively.</td>', 'I like the shot, but I have a hard time figuring out exactly how it fits in the rust category -- except maybe figuratively.', '2004-05-10 22:04:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(710180, 74479, 11895, '<td valign="top">nice colors and DoF</td>', 'nice colors and DoF', '2004-05-10 22:05:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(710183, 73963, 3080, '<td valign="top">Very nice find.  You know what I wish though?  I wish that you could desaturate all but the inside of the umbrella.  This would be a perfect example of that technique I think.  The only problem would be the orange thing on the right side of the photo, which I find distracting to the umbrella.  I do realize that it''s rusty too, and adds to the rustness of the photo, but I just think it takes away from this beautiful find.  Rusty, and interesting.  Congrats.  Focus and clarity are really good and I like the placement of the subject as well.  Slightly close crop on the left side, kind of nipped off one of the corners of the umbrella.  What would something like this be used for?  Strange indeed. ~Heather~</td>', 'Very nice find.  You know what I wish though?  I wish that you could desaturate all but the inside of the umbrella.  This would be a perfect example of that technique I think.  The only problem would be the orange thing on the right side of the photo, which I find distracting to the umbrella.  I do realize that it''s rusty too, and adds to the rustness of the photo, but I just think it takes away from this beautiful find.  Rusty, and interesting.  Congrats.  Focus and clarity are really good and I like the placement of the subject as well.  Slightly close crop on the left side, kind of nipped off one of the corners of the umbrella.  What would something like this be used for?  Strange indeed. ~Heather~', '2004-05-10 22:06:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(710188, 74540, 3080, '<td valign="top">Well, this is definately interesting, but I''m not really sure what I''m looking at, or where the rust is.  Are the things sticking out of the ball rusty?  Or are the chains?  What about the fence thingy behind the ball?  I can see a lot of things that COULD be rusted, but not sure if I really see the actual rust or not.  I like the DOF, and I think that the streaks add to the interest of the shot.  Rain?  The darkness is also nice. ~Heather~</td>', 'Well, this is definately interesting, but I''m not really sure what I''m looking at, or where the rust is.  Are the things sticking out of the ball rusty?  Or are the chains?  What about the fence thingy behind the ball?  I can see a lot of things that COULD be rusted, but not sure if I really see the actual rust or not.  I like the DOF, and I think that the streaks add to the interest of the shot.  Rain?  The darkness is also nice. ~Heather~', '2004-05-10 22:09:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(710194, 73385, 3080, '<td valign="top">Strange place for a bolt.  Definately rusty.  I think that the DOF is good, and it works for the shot.  I like the different colors of rust, and the texture as well.  were you able to take different angles of this?  head on, dead center seems less interesting that a dramatic angle, but sometimes its just not possible.  would like to at least see it as an option though.  lighting seems good, and overall interesting rust.  ~Heather~</td>', 'Strange place for a bolt.  Definately rusty.  I think that the DOF is good, and it works for the shot.  I like the different colors of rust, and the texture as well.  were you able to take different angles of this?  head on, dead center seems less interesting that a dramatic angle, but sometimes its just not possible.  would like to at least see it as an option though.  lighting seems good, and overall interesting rust.  ~Heather~', '2004-05-10 22:11:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(710196, 74380, 11895, '<td valign="top">depth of field is too shallow, more of the subject should be in focus, nice colors</td>', 'depth of field is too shallow, more of the subject should be in focus, nice colors', '2004-05-10 22:12:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(710198, 74143, 3080, '<td valign="top">odd place for an iron elephant. lol.  I like how well he stands out on the blue sky.  very nice job picking day and time to shoot this elephant.  focus and clarity are good, and I like the placement of the subject within the photo.  did you try different angles or placements?  I wonder how this would look with a slight boost of saturation?  something to try anyway.  I like it. ~Heather~</td>', 'odd place for an iron elephant. lol.  I like how well he stands out on the blue sky.  very nice job picking day and time to shoot this elephant.  focus and clarity are good, and I like the placement of the subject within the photo.  did you try different angles or placements?  I wonder how this would look with a slight boost of saturation?  something to try anyway.  I like it. ~Heather~', '2004-05-10 22:13:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(710210, 74203, 11895, '<td valign="top">great title for this image</td>', 'great title for this image', '2004-05-10 22:22:17.000000', NULL, 1),
