(713402, 73492, 12252, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Glen King:</b></div><hr/><i> Not a bad idea. Interesting composition. If you''re going to take this route, I think you might do better to try the old National Lampoon magazine cover, "if you don''t buy this magazine, we''ll shoot this dog!"   8 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wasn''t that Mad Magazine?</td>', 'Originally posted by Glen King: Not a bad idea. Interesting composition. If you''re going to take this route, I think you might do better to try the old National Lampoon magazine cover, "if you don''t buy this magazine, we''ll shoot this dog!"   8   Wasn''t that Mad Magazine?', '2004-05-12 04:54:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(713421, 73708, 17149, '<td valign="top">thank you for your comments. i will really take note of the criticisms and try to improve my work next time. <br/> <br/>i really should have moved closer to the sculpture to get a better shot, but i was worried of the guard watching me getting my feet on the grass. :) i have so limited options on moving left or right, because there are procession carts (covered with bright-colored plastic sheets) on both sides, a few meters from the sculpture. weren''t those carts there, i could have gotten a better background, i.e. the ruin''s balcony, which is a lot creepier.<br/> <br/>this is my first entry to DPC. i''m still glad it got to this place. i still got a lot to learn hopefully with your help. :)<br/> <br/>again... thanks.</td>', 'thank you for your comments. i will really take note of the criticisms and try to improve my work next time.  i really should have moved closer to the sculpture to get a better shot, but i was worried of the guard watching me getting my feet on the grass. :) i have so limited options on moving left or right, because there are procession carts (covered with bright-colored plastic sheets) on both sides, a few meters from the sculpture. weren''t those carts there, i could have gotten a better background, i.e. the ruin''s balcony, which is a lot creepier. this is my first entry to DPC. i''m still glad it got to this place. i still got a lot to learn hopefully with your help. :) again... thanks.', '2004-05-12 04:58:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(713434, 73494, 16907, '<td valign="top">27 out of 443, not too bad... Thank you all for your kind comments. If it was easy to win a ribbon every time, it wouldn''t be that much fun :)<br/>ok, here we go again</td>', '27 out of 443, not too bad... Thank you all for your kind comments. If it was easy to win a ribbon every time, it wouldn''t be that much fun :)ok, here we go again', '2004-05-12 05:12:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(713435, 74246, 18722, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all the commenters.<br/> <br/>Well, this actually did much better than I expected it to.  I had been playing with exposure settings instead of just taking the shot, and I ran out of daylight.  This was taken too late in the day for a crisp image, and resulted in needed a bit more light than what was available -- and all I had to use was the on-camera flash.  This photo was the best of the bunch composition-wise, but it was not good in contrast and since I am even less experienced with photoshop than I am with my camera I over did it on a number of things.  I over sharpened for one, and in an effort to handle the poor lighting I added a lot of noise.  Trying to use NeatImage to handle the noise resulted in the loss of nearly all texture.<br/> <br/>The nest: yes it was placed -- but I did find it on another of these things (I may live in a farming community, but a farmer I am not).  Unfortunately, the nest had been abandoned for a couple of days, and the weather during the taking of the photo and the previous day were much too cold for the eggs to be on there own.  Had it been an active nest I would have used a ladder or something to get up to the level, but since it was abandoned I moved it to a similar place with other rusting farm machinery that I could climb up onto.  So, while it was placed for the photo, it was actually in such a place to begin with.<br/> <br/>Again, thanks to those who commented.<br/> <br/>David</td>', 'Thanks to all the commenters. Well, this actually did much better than I expected it to.  I had been playing with exposure settings instead of just taking the shot, and I ran out of daylight.  This was taken too late in the day for a crisp image, and resulted in needed a bit more light than what was available -- and all I had to use was the on-camera flash.  This photo was the best of the bunch composition-wise, but it was not good in contrast and since I am even less experienced with photoshop than I am with my camera I over did it on a number of things.  I over sharpened for one, and in an effort to handle the poor lighting I added a lot of noise.  Trying to use NeatImage to handle the noise resulted in the loss of nearly all texture. The nest: yes it was placed -- but I did find it on another of these things (I may live in a farming community, but a farmer I am not).  Unfortunately, the nest had been abandoned for a couple of days, and the weather during the taking of the photo and the previous day were much too cold for the eggs to be on there own.  Had it been an active nest I would have used a ladder or something to get up to the level, but since it was abandoned I moved it to a similar place with other rusting farm machinery that I could climb up onto.  So, while it was placed for the photo, it was actually in such a place to begin with. Again, thanks to those who commented. David', '2004-05-12 05:15:43.000000', NULL, 0),
