(713958, 74293, 5086, '<td valign="top">Thank you very much for the positive comments.  I entered close to the end of the challenge, picking my picture from what I had taken during the week, with no knowledge beforehand of the weeks challenge; and sent it with no editing.  I was very pleased to be given such high marks overall when I had put no thought or extra effort into searching for the right shot...  in fact, not even knowing the topic.</td>', 'Thank you very much for the positive comments.  I entered close to the end of the challenge, picking my picture from what I had taken during the week, with no knowledge beforehand of the weeks challenge; and sent it with no editing.  I was very pleased to be given such high marks overall when I had put no thought or extra effort into searching for the right shot...  in fact, not even knowing the topic.', '2004-05-12 12:02:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(714016, 73843, 18419, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone!  What I liked about it was that the bridge was solid and clean, even though it was rust-covered. As Dusty mentioned, that was (probably; I didn''t notice a company name on it) the intent of the designers.  The idea for the the DOF and adjustments to the view angle are spot on; I really, really appreciate these suggestions to help make me a better photographer.<br/>Thanks again<br/>Stuart<br/></td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone!  What I liked about it was that the bridge was solid and clean, even though it was rust-covered. As Dusty mentioned, that was (probably; I didn''t notice a company name on it) the intent of the designers.  The idea for the the DOF and adjustments to the view angle are spot on; I really, really appreciate these suggestions to help make me a better photographer.Thanks againStuart', '2004-05-12 12:29:26.000000', NULL, 0),
